{
 "description": "A 100 x 100 x 30 block, a recess 88 x 88 x 12 deep from the top (z 18..30), then one cut from the bottom whose profile is the ring between a 95 x 95 and a 68 x 68 rectangle, 17.5 deep. A 0.5 mm floor (z 17.5..18) is left joining the outer wall to the 68 x 68 x 18 inner block, but the cut gave two bodies, the inner block and a rest 3411.9 mm3 short (#545). Cutting the ring before the recess gives the right part. Result: one body, 100*100*30 - 88*88*12 - (95^2 - 68^2)*17.5 = 130054.5 mm3.",
 "commands": [
